WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:02.689
Diesels are highly popular in Ukraine.

00:00:02.689 --> 00:00:09.150
This Volkswagen Passat has just arrived from
Germany - it meets Euro-5 emissions standards.

00:00:09.150 --> 00:00:11.929
Some mechanics take a close look at it.

00:00:11.929 --> 00:00:16.800
They know it'll need adapting to Ukranian
standards within a few months at the latest.

00:00:16.800 --> 00:00:22.250
That's when they'll have to remove its catalytic
converter.

00:00:22.250 --> 00:00:25.720
The catalytic converters and the particle
filters often cause problems.

00:00:25.720 --> 00:00:29.070
They get clogged up very quickly and stop
working.

00:00:29.070 --> 00:00:32.899
The diesel quality's too low here.

00:00:32.899 --> 00:00:37.329
Without emissions control systems the diesels
pump unfiltered toxic gases and particles

00:00:37.329 --> 00:00:39.410
straight into the air.

00:00:39.410 --> 00:00:44.440
And because regular inspections for cars are
not legally required in Ukraine, exhaust systems

00:00:44.440 --> 00:00:46.600
can be manipulated without fear of detection.

00:00:46.600 --> 00:00:52.050
It's easy for experienced mechanics to remove
an exhaust emissions control unit - and replace

00:00:52.050 --> 00:00:54.430
it with a section of plain pipe.

00:00:54.430 --> 00:00:56.230
This component comes from a Renault diesel.

00:00:56.230 --> 00:01:02.140
If a catalytic converter is clogged up, the
vehicle won't start.

00:01:02.140 --> 00:01:04.620
We hook it up with the diagnostic computer.

00:01:04.620 --> 00:01:08.410
The problem is very often a clogged up catalytic
converter.

00:01:08.410 --> 00:01:13.860
Sometimes we cut the converter out, sometimes
we can repair it.

00:01:13.860 --> 00:01:19.580
The Ukrainian city of Lutsk has a population
of 240 thousand.

00:01:19.580 --> 00:01:21.120
The air is foul.

00:01:21.120 --> 00:01:24.970
And 82 percent of the pollution comes from
cars and trucks.

00:01:24.970 --> 00:01:29.530
There's an automarket here twice a month - trading
mostly diesels.

00:01:29.530 --> 00:01:33.460
Private operators import the cars, mostly
from Germany.

00:01:33.460 --> 00:01:37.470
Diesels meeting older emissions standards
which get registered in Poland or Lithuania

00:01:37.470 --> 00:01:41.020
are treated as transit vehicles for up to
a year.

00:01:41.020 --> 00:01:48.040
Only the later Euro-5 standard cars are actually
allowed to be imported.

00:01:48.040 --> 00:01:53.900
Germany worries about the environment and
that's why the price of diesels is falling.

00:01:53.900 --> 00:02:03.000
Germany understands its people and spends
a lot of money on environmental protection.

00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:08.679
Throughout the city a number of stations are
constantly measuring air quality.

00:02:08.679 --> 00:02:14.060
The results show that only two other Ukrainian
cities have filthier air than here.

00:02:14.060 --> 00:02:22.180
And now Lutsk is filling up with sub-standard
German diesels.

00:02:22.180 --> 00:02:27.349
The air will most certainly become dirtier,
because diesel's a fuel that is so bad for

00:02:27.349 --> 00:02:30.900
the environment.

00:02:30.900 --> 00:02:35.360
Diesels have become hard to sell in Germany,
and now they're flooding into eastern European

00:02:35.360 --> 00:02:36.489
markets.

00:02:36.489 --> 00:02:40.319
The Germans have simply outsourced their diesel
emissions problems.

